<h1>Video Editing Performance on Apple Silicon</h1>
<p>
  For video editing, not all specs are created equal. While CPU and GPU cores are important, the key to significant performance gains in Final Cut Pro and DaVinci Resolve lies in Apple's dedicated hardware accelerators: the Media Engines.
</p>
<p>
  The table below focuses on the specifications most critical for video editing: ProRes and H.264/HEVC encode/decode engines, GPU core count, and memory bandwidth. These directly impact timeline fluidity, export speeds, and the ability to work with high-resolution, professional-grade codecs.
</p>

